WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.880
With a population of 14 million,

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.800
Kinshasa is the largest French-speaking city in the world.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.120
The streets are full of activity.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.400
Many people get up very early,

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:13.760
at around 5 a.m.,

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.000
and take on several jobs during the day to get by.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:20.760
Africa News,

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.000
Palmares,

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.000
Machete,

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:23.760
Le Fas,

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.040
Referance.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:26.560
They can be couriers.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:29.280
Sweepers,

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:31.960
maggot sellers,

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.640
or even jewelers.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:40.640
At midday,

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:41.840
they count their money,

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.480
often dreaming of making a fortune.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.040
They even dream of wealth in this slum,

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:56.240
like 80%

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:57.720
of its inhabitants.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:00.880
Albert,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:01.600
a fisherman,

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.440
lives on less than £1.50 per day.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:08.000
The country's richest people live just opposite him.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.760
That's La Cité du Fleuve

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:19.440
They are rich, and we are poor.
They are doing business, we are fishing.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:24.120
This apartment complex is reserved for the new upper class,

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.680
and of course the millionaires of the Democratic Republic of Congo.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.840
It's impossible for anyone from the outside to get in.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:46.400
Fale Ipupa is one of these hugely wealthy people that the rest of the country dreams of becoming.

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:51.760
Never in my wildest dream when I was a kid could
I have imagined having cars and all these things.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.440
Just from singing, and being recognised
in Kinshasa and then all over Africa.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:01.600
Fale Ipupa is the most famous singer in the Democratic Republic of Congo.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.840
He performs all over the world with international stars,

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.480
and he is a multi-millionaire.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:07.840
uidas

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.360
adidas

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:10.920
Guy,

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:11.080
I love you,

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:11.120
man.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:14.120
I love you too.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:14.520
My love,

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:14.840
Fally Pupa,

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:15.000
you know.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.160
What you saying?

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.720
Hey.

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:22.880
He has just invested over 600,000 pounds for his new home in this Riverside estate.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:27.200
Are the doors open?
Go on, open them!

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.400
I really like being here, especially on Sundays.
It's relaxing.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:41.520
I love our river and I come here often with friends
and family, so I decided to lay a few bricks.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:46.280
Just a few bricks makes this Californian-style villa,

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.640
which stands out hugely here in the Congo,

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:51.160
the eighth poorest country in the world.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.320
His neighbors are lawyers,

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:54.360
financiers,

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:55.440
or entrepreneurs.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:58.360
who have made their fortune selling raw materials,

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.840
which the rest of the world is snapping up.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:06.440
The Congo's underground reserves are full of wealth and boost the economy.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.640
These people are very wealthy.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.840
They could live in London or Miami,

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:12.920
but they've chosen to stay here.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:17.440
That's good.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.600
Folly likes to relax far away from the hustle and bustle of the city center.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.320
The Congo River,

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:29.960
one of the longest in the world,

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:31.600
is the city's playground.

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.680
But it's also a source of livelihood for fishermen,

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.560
who have quickly recognized him.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.040
Fally! Please can you help us at all?

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:49.920
They say they're my brothers, they want
a bit of money, I have to give it to them.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.160
Give them 50 dollars.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.200
Fali gets a port employee to distribute a few notes among them.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:04.480
That's a lot. We shouted Fally, Fally, and he
gave us 50 dollars to share between us six.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:08.000
It's the equivalent of six pounds per fisherman,

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.760
which is the same as an entire working week.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:16.480
These people have different problems from us.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:23.120
They even work on Sundays and if I have
the opportunity to give a little something...

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:30.720
...even if it's just so that they can take
something home for their children...

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:34.000
I will always be happy to do it.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:51.680
The Democratic Republic of Congo is the largest country in Central Africa.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.000
It's four times the size of France.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.960
It has been ravaged repeatedly by war for almost

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:00.880
60 years,

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.720
which has resulted in over 6 million deaths.

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.120
The country is also under a dictatorship.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:09.880
Mobutu Seziseko,

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:12.360
nicknamed the Leopard of Zaire,

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.760
was in power for 32 years.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.800
While ruling the country with an iron fist,

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.280
he embezzled 4 billion pounds.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:22.600
In 1996,

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:24.200
a civil war broke out.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:32.040
Militias supported by neighboring countries enlisted thousands of child soldiers to try and seize the country's wealth.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:33.160
Mobutu,

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:33.800
meanwhile,

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.800
eventually died in exile.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.640
Another emblematic president in the early

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:40.720
2000s was Joseph Kabila.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:46.360
He accumulated more than 11 billion pounds during his 18 years in power.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:50.280
He returned to power in January 2019.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:51.480
Today,

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:55.160
entire regions are still unstable in this huge country.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:57.680
Everything still needs to be built,

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:01.560
and some businessmen make their fortune amid this chaos.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:08.640
In the Congo, you can wake up
poor in the morning...

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:11.520
...and become rich the following day
because you have worked.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:19.080
Eric has a huge project at the end of this extremely dangerous road.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:25.920
He is erecting a huge dam to provide the population with electricity.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:30.000
It's going to bring in almost
one million dollars per month.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.120
In the east of the country,

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.960
the Great Lakes region is one of its most beautiful areas,

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.200
but also one of the most dangerous in Africa,

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:39.160
having been in almost permanent war for over 20 years.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:39.880
Robert,

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.000
a former rebel leader,

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.200
has become a businessman.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:43.680
He is also a politician.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:50.000
When you're a member of parliament,
politics doesn't stop us from doing business.

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:52.680
Robert built his fortune in coltan mines.

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:56.760
This is an essential ore for the manufacturing of mobile phones.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:01.520
A small town has been created thanks to this businessman's employment.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:02.680
And every day,

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:05.760
3,000 miners also dream of a better life.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:13.200
When I see this car, I tell myself that I could have
one like that some day, if God grants me the means.

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:17.360
The Congo's underground wealth has really boosted the economy.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:19.680
An upper class is emerging,

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.000
and in Kinshasa,

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:22.000
the capital,

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.440
new products are appearing.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:27.600
This orange juice costs almost 20 pounds.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:32.560
But the majority of the population is still extremely poor.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:34.680
With such disadvantage,

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.960
these people find refuge in religion,

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:40.200
which provides a windfall for corrupt pastors,

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:45.360
who have practically become stars by selling miracle cures at a high price.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:51.760
This cures many diseases, even AIDS.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:59.880
We have traveled to one of the most chaotic countries in Africa to understand how its people managed to get by,

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:03.440
and sometimes even managed to build huge fortunes.

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:09.440
In Kinshasa,

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.000
the roads resemble like battered tracks.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:16.600
They're difficult to navigate.

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:21.960
In this huge mess,

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:24.280
a young woman is fighting for her future.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:26.080
She is called Mukembe.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:37.520
They are law enforcement officers, we are
supposed to follow what they say...

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:42.800
Yet here I am in front of two officers,
one who is telling me to go to the left...

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:47.040
and the other to go to the right.
What am I supposed to do?

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:49.760
Boukembe is in the middle of a test.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:51.280
Sat in the back,

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:57.360
Arnaud must evaluate her ability to sneak through traffic and put a bit of pressure on her.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:07.120
After you turn again, take a right here.
You don't know the road apparently.

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:10.800
Turn left, go ahead, follow the car.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:14.920
Gokhebi has applied for a job as a driver in a start-up company.

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:24.040
The company was created by a Congolese businesswoman who wants to lift women out of poverty and is recognizable by its pink cars.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.600
Okembe was a nurse until this point.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.400
If she passes the test,

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:32.120
she will triple her salary,

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:34.560
raising it to 200 pounds per month.

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:45.600
can't wait to start my job, let's hope
it's all gone OK and I've passed the test.

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:49.680
We will go around and then go back to the office.

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:52.760
To give herself the best chance,

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:56.000
Mukambi stays in character right until the end.

00:09:56.600 --> 00:10:00.000
But it will be a few days until she finds out if she has got the right person.

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:04.520
There are already about 15 cars in the company's car park.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:09.560
The startup wants to create high-end services for the middle and upper class.

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:11.480
There are drinks,

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:12.080
cakes,

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:18.200
and even a Wi-Fi connection to allow clients to work while they sit in Kinshasa's traffic jams.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:26.640
You don't find things like that around here.
We have come up with it.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:31.640
Patricia is a businesswoman who wants to promote female integration.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:34.040
After studying in South Africa,

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:35.680
she returned to the Congo.

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:40.080
She has created her driver's service with the help of investors.

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:42.200
She also supports new businesses.

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:47.520
We want to have millionaires.
The Congo is rich.

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:52.480
We have more than 80 million people living here,
we have resources above and below ground...

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:58.640
...and it's time for Congolese women
to take advantage of this wealth.

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:02.080
Despite the instability all over her country...

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:05.360
Give me both, yes two thighs.

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:10.520
Patricia wants to show the whole world that the Democratic Republic of Congo can take off.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:14.880
The Congo can't be reduced to rapes and wars.

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:21.600
No, there are young people, young women like us
who are trying to make a change...

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:26.640
So it's wrong that people reduce the Congo
to a place where 'things do not work...

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:32.320
things don't evolve' no, it's this new generation
who are going to improve the country.

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:37.160
Just like Patricia and her friends who are banking on the future of their country,

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:42.960
many Congolese people return to work and invest in their country after years of living abroad,

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:46.160
especially in Europe or the United States.

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:48.240
These repatriates,

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:49.480
as they are called,

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:54.560
live in secure areas where they can find all of the comforts that they were used to abroad.

00:11:58.840 --> 00:12:00.080
At La Cité de Fleuve,

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:07.120
the complex of high-end apartment buildings and villas extend over 300 hectares and two new people are moving in.

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:10.880
Olivier and Naomi.

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:14.760
A few days ago they were still living in Johannesburg,

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:15.480
South Africa.

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:28.880
The washing machine is really the number
one priority, right darling? And the bed!

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:32.600
Olivier and Naomi work in finance.

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:37.280
They decided to return to their country because there are new professional activities.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:44.400
The living room will go there, a small
living room, a small living room...

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:52.080
And a carpet there, a table, and a TV.
That's our room.

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:56.440
And it has a breathtaking view of the Congo River.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:13:01.200
Olivier and Naomi got married in Kinshasa just three days ago,

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:03.440
and they want to start their family here.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.160
The couple earn 3,000 pounds a month,

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:08.480
which is over 100 times the average.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:12.640
The rental loan costs almost 1,000 pounds,

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:15.480
but that's the price you pay for security.

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:18.560
I'm in a place where my kids can play in the street,

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:19.200
The project has already successfully passed all of the feasibility tests.

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:22.680
and they don't have to worry about a hundred other people on the street,

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:24.480
and they don't have to worry about air pollution,

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:25.480
noise pollution.

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:27.560
They can do their homework in peace.

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:29.600
So it's also very much about the environment,

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:30.560
but also,

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:30.960
yes,

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:33.920
it is a whole lot safer than the inner city.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:38.400
We have a brand new spotless apartment..

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:46.160
...we will have brand new appliances and I'm
waiting for my little one who will also be new!

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:50.480
Olivier and Naomi have found their safe haven.

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:53.600
Beginning of a new life for us.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:54.080
Yes.

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:58.040
Demand to live in this new residence is growing.

00:13:58.400 --> 00:13:58.920
Eventually,

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:02.640
La Cité du Fleuve will have more than 2,000 homes,

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:05.400
including that of the singer Fali'i Poupas.

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:15.160
We find him in a large house,

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:19.120
which he has rented as the backdrop of his new music video.

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:26.800
2, 1, 0 Action!

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:31.720
The extras are dressed up as Congolese warriors.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:37.280
The day starts well for Fali,

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:38.760
but all of a sudden,

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:40.080
the music stops,

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.480
for there has been a power cut in the area.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:50.320
There's no electricity, we are trying
to manage it to see what we can do.

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:53.280
Fali and his team are stuck.

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:00.000
Finally,

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:03.480
A technician manages to get his hands on a generator,

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:05.600
but that quickly breaks down too.

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:13.520
Folly is desperate,

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:16.520
even though he is used to such disappointment.

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:26.560
Look, I'm Congolese, that's to say,
I was born and raised here...

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:30.880
So we cannot leave the country
just because there are power cuts.

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:32.360
Manon,

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:34.200
Falehipupa's assistant,

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:37.440
uses the car's sound system to finish filming the clip.

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:43.120
We make it all with tiny budgets. We will connect
it to the car while we wait for the current.

00:15:43.360 --> 00:15:44.800
We have no choice.

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:46.720
Thanks to this trick,

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:48.880
shooting can finish without a hitch.

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:51.600
In his 20-year career,

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.000
Folly has earned several million pounds.

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:56.080
He has had a huge success,

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:59.120
which is not necessarily an anomaly in this country.

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:11.520
Congo's underground is rich in minerals,

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:14.920
which have helped make the fortune of several well-advised men.

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:18.160
One of the main resources is coltan.

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:19.280
which,

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:21.040
once it's been transformed,

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:24.360
is used in the manufacturing of mobile phones.

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:28.040
The mines are in the Great Lakes region,

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:29.560
in the east of the country,

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:30.960
on the Rwandan border.

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:34.160
In Goma,

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:35.760
the capital of North Kivu,

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:38.760
conflicts have been raging for over 20 years.

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:41.760
Armed groups are trying to seize the land's wealth.

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:49.400
The UN permanently deploys 16,000 peacekeepers to maintain a semblance of peace in the region.

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:51.880
The region is very poor,

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:55.680
traumatized by successive rebellions and massacres.

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:57.880
Those who have made their fortune,

00:16:58.280 --> 00:16:59.880
especially in raw materials,

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:02.160
live in the luxurious Lake Kivu.

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:08.800
One of the region's most important businessmen lives in this huge villa.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:13.520
There is a watchtower with a huge police presence at the entrance.

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:15.680
It's a true fortress.

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:19.160
Its owner has several tens of millions of pounds.

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:24.800
How are you, François?

00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:25.840
sir.

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:28.680
Robert Seninga is the king of the Coltan mines.

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:30.800
He has had an eventful life.

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:31.880
Formerly,

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:33.080
he was a rebel leader.

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:33.840
Today,

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:37.640
he is a businessman and also a member of the Maissi Parliament,

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:39.640
a district near Tagoma.

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:46.960
When you're a politician, politics
doesn't stop you from doing business.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:53.040
He even admits that his power has helped him to become an owner of some of these mines.

00:17:54.080 --> 00:18:01.000
Robert Seninga is also the president of one of the largest corporations extracting Clotin in this region.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:06.680
He is always escorted by armed guards as he regularly receives threats.

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:19.520
Where are we?
This is the corporation's headquarters.

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:26.480
This is the head office.
This is where the trading takes place.

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:29.400
The building does not pay for the mine,

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:33.000
but the cooperative earns millions in turnover every year.

00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:37.200
Hello, how are you?

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:41.520
Robert Seninga gives an update on coltan production over the last few days.

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:46.800
On the 6th, we got 4 tons 668 kilos in total.

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:48.720
And the numbers are pretty good.

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:54.480
We are swimming in 40 tons.

00:18:54.640 --> 00:18:56.960
And so what's the revenue on that?

00:18:57.120 --> 00:19:01.760
A kilo is 42-45 dollars.

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:05.600
You have the figure, you have the figure...

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:11.520
Robert Seninga prefers to remain discreet.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:13.400
These last few days,

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:17.240
the mines have given a lot to the cooperative and to their owners,

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:19.160
almost 2 million pounds.

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:24.400
The businessman employs 3,000 people to achieve these results.

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:27.000
He claims to be a faultless boss.

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:28.160
Are there any children working in your mines?

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:28.800
ayama bwiriza
lyi ndiyo namna inayo kubungabunga
Are there any'children working in your mines?

00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:30.480
Are there any children working in your mines?
imba madini

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:33.200
No, there are no children because it's forbidden.

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:37.600
There are officers who are responsible for ensuring
that children do not end up in there.

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:40.560
Children should be in school, not the mines.

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:43.880
Helmets,

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:44.440
boots,

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:47.880
and masks are mandatory in the mines to ensure the workers'

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:48.240
safety.

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:50.480
In fact,

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:53.360
the site could be a model example for the region.

00:19:58.720 --> 00:19:59.960
These mines are situa-

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:09.680
It's 60 kilometers from Goma in a beautiful region of North Kivu with hills and pastures as far as the eye can see.

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:26.400
It is also one of the most dangerous regions in Africa.

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:30.640
It has been at war for over 25 years.

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:34.680
In 1995,

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:38.560
one of the worst tragedies of the 20th century broke out in Rwanda.

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:42.840
A genocide which would kill almost one million people.

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:48.400
Hundreds of thousands of survivors fled to the neighboring Democratic Republic of Congo,

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:50.840
and North Kivu in particular.

00:20:52.840 --> 00:20:56.520
But militants who took part in the massacre joined the exodus.

00:20:57.320 --> 00:20:57.800
Since then,

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:01.920
this region in the east of the Congo has been extremely volatile.

00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:04.760
Dozens of rebel groups are clashing,

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:06.240
and in particular,

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:10.280
they are trying to capture some of the Congolese underground wealth.

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:21.240
Landry Robertseninga's chief engineer accompanies us to his mines.

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:32.560
Seninga has saved the local community, Maisi,
because thanks to him, life can go on as normal.

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:40.200
Yet little seems to have changed in the region in recent years.

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:46.520
The road is in a terrible state.

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:47.640
Every day,

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:50.160
people risk their lives in order to work.

00:21:54.920 --> 00:21:57.200
Our car struggles to get to the ravine,

00:21:57.720 --> 00:22:00.920
despite several attempts due to crevices full of water.

00:22:08.080 --> 00:22:10.080
We were seconds away!

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:15.600
Otherwise we would have ended up in this river
and had been in serious trouble.

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:19.400
Fatal

00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:21.560
accidents are common on this road.

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:26.400
Nice, we've been saved!

00:22:27.920 --> 00:22:31.960
It will take us a total of five hours to travel just 60 kilometers.

00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:34.800
We've arrived.

00:22:36.640 --> 00:22:37.520
This is Rubaiya,

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:39.440
a town near the mining site.

00:22:40.160 --> 00:22:41.720
The town has boomed recently,

00:22:42.120 --> 00:22:44.560
growing exponentially in just a few years.

00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:46.040
Today,

00:22:46.320 --> 00:22:47.880
10,000 people live here,

00:22:48.520 --> 00:22:50.800
practically cut off from the outside world.

00:22:51.400 --> 00:22:52.800
Life is organized.

00:22:53.680 --> 00:22:55.200
There's a sewing workshop,

00:22:55.600 --> 00:22:56.440
a hairdresser's,

00:22:56.760 --> 00:23:00.360
and even something that's turned its inside into a nightclub.

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:02.000
In Robaya,

00:23:02.440 --> 00:23:10.360
everything has been created to meet the needs of the population that has come to take advantage of this new Congolese wild west.

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:15.920
Robert Seninga's face is displayed everywhere.

00:23:16.680 --> 00:23:17.680
According to Landry,

00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:19.160
his loyal follower,

00:23:19.480 --> 00:23:21.600
he can make all dreams possible.

00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:25.120
Here is where the first miner lived.

00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:30.240
He was the first person to start working in
the first hole that was discovered in Rubaya.

00:23:30.400 --> 00:23:33.920
He managed to build this beautiful house
which you see here.

00:23:37.280 --> 00:23:39.320
miracle seems to be taking place.

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:41.800
But upon closer look,

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:44.200
most homes are simple wooden shacks.

00:23:45.840 --> 00:23:48.800
Jou lives here with his wife and their three children.

00:23:49.920 --> 00:23:53.120
With five people living in 15 square meters of space,

00:23:53.480 --> 00:23:55.080
they are forced to be very tidy.

00:23:56.000 --> 00:24:01.360
The house is very small.
We hang the shoes on the wall.

00:24:01.520 --> 00:24:05.920
And we put the children's clothes over there.

00:24:08.200 --> 00:24:08.960
In the other room,

00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:11.240
the kitchen is attached to the family bed.

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:16.720
The bed is really small.

00:24:17.200 --> 00:24:21.520
We sleep there and my wife cooks here.

00:24:22.880 --> 00:24:24.720
The couple moved here five years ago,

00:24:25.280 --> 00:24:28.360
when Gilles wanted to earn his fortune in the mines.

00:24:28.880 --> 00:24:32.720
When I see this car I tell myself that I
could have one like that one day...

00:24:32.880 --> 00:24:35.200
...if God granted me the means to do so.

00:24:37.400 --> 00:24:37.800
For now,

00:24:38.080 --> 00:24:40.400
Gilles only earns five euros per day.

00:24:43.360 --> 00:24:48.960
He works 10 kilometers from the center of Urbaya and must travel for an hour and a half to get there.

00:24:56.640 --> 00:24:59.960
Hundreds of coltan extraction sites surround the area.

00:25:03.400 --> 00:25:05.000
Jiz is called Bamfu.

00:25:06.800 --> 00:25:07.320
Every day,

00:25:07.640 --> 00:25:11.840
it filters Khotan mixed with sand that is extracted from the mine.

00:25:23.120 --> 00:25:30.080
It's easier to sort the coltan by hand,
so we are able to separate it from the sand.

00:25:30.680 --> 00:25:32.840
Coltan is this black substance.

00:25:33.160 --> 00:25:34.120
Once transformed,

00:25:34.280 --> 00:25:37.720
it goes into the manufacturing of micro-electronic components.

00:25:37.920 --> 00:25:41.920
That's the coltan.
That's what goes into mobile phones.

00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:44.520
Later on,

00:25:44.840 --> 00:25:47.040
Jill has to go into the mine to dig.

00:25:47.480 --> 00:25:48.880
The wall is very slippery.

00:25:51.920 --> 00:25:54.560
Wait.
Stop!

00:25:54.800 --> 00:25:59.520
Going down isn't difficult if you look after yourself.

00:26:01.120 --> 00:26:04.360
And there's no safety measure to rely on along this

00:26:05.000 --> 00:26:05.760
15-meter descent.

00:26:06.880 --> 00:26:08.240
Once you've arrived at the bottom,

00:26:08.520 --> 00:26:10.000
it is difficult to breathe.

00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:13.400
Tons of sand have already been extracted,

00:26:13.800 --> 00:26:15.240
which has opened up tunnels.

00:26:16.080 --> 00:26:18.440
There is no supporting structure to secure them.

00:26:19.320 --> 00:26:21.640
so the risk of a landslide is very high.

00:26:24.320 --> 00:26:27.960
Zhiyu extracts the coltan using just his hands.

00:26:31.520 --> 00:26:37.680
There is a lot of sand here. It's endless.
There's really a lot.

00:26:44.560 --> 00:26:46.720
Priority is given to extraction,

00:26:47.280 --> 00:26:48.040
never safety.

00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:51.560
There are regular accidents in these mines.

00:26:58.240 --> 00:27:02.960
It's very dangerous to be here, right?
It's brittle but it's well-developed.

00:27:04.040 --> 00:27:04.680
But Landry,

00:27:05.280 --> 00:27:05.800
our guide,

00:27:05.920 --> 00:27:07.120
doesn't see the problem.

00:27:08.320 --> 00:27:10.560
In Rubaya mines and wherever we work..

00:27:10.720 --> 00:27:14.240
.there are cases where we have recorded deaths, case

00:27:14.400 --> 00:27:17.120
...cases of landslides, and that's
why there can be deaths.

00:27:17.280 --> 00:27:22.560
Imagine if this thing rushed towards us
like that, we would suffocate.

00:27:22.720 --> 00:27:25.520
There are some who can resist
and others who cannot.

00:27:26.840 --> 00:27:28.640
There are no official figures,

00:27:28.840 --> 00:27:32.280
but men regularly lose their lives extracting Clotin.

00:27:43.360 --> 00:27:44.800
How old are you?

00:27:44.960 --> 00:27:46.240
I'm twenty years old.

00:27:46.400 --> 00:27:48.960
He's twenty years old,
you can see him...

00:27:52.400 --> 00:27:54.800
Here, you can see that he's thin.

00:27:54.960 --> 00:28:00.880
I can see why someone might think that
he's too young, but he is paid for his work.

00:28:03.120 --> 00:28:05.000
Auger's 30 or so colleagues,

00:28:05.240 --> 00:28:06.000
at least half,

00:28:06.120 --> 00:28:08.160
don't seem to be older than teenagers.

00:28:08.920 --> 00:28:10.920
This site isn't an anomaly.

00:28:11.640 --> 00:28:15.080
We meet a lot of children in the region who hide from the camera.

00:28:16.080 --> 00:28:17.200
According to UNICEF,

00:28:17.440 --> 00:28:20.440
mines allegedly employ 40,000 children.

00:28:22.640 --> 00:28:23.240
This mineral,

00:28:23.360 --> 00:28:24.960
which is generating fortunes,

00:28:25.360 --> 00:28:29.680
steals these children's childhood and sometimes even their lives.

00:28:38.480 --> 00:28:39.640
Two months before filming,

00:28:39.920 --> 00:28:43.240
a massacre took place one evening in the center of Rubaya.

00:28:44.680 --> 00:28:47.960
Three men armed with machetes launched an attack.

00:28:49.720 --> 00:28:50.760
Twelve were killed,

00:28:51.120 --> 00:28:54.200
including three women and a five-year-old child.

00:28:55.360 --> 00:29:01.080
It was undoubtedly a settling of scores over the Khotan black market that plagues the region.

00:29:02.160 --> 00:29:06.480
Underground reselling of Khotan happens at all levels of the production chain,

00:29:06.960 --> 00:29:09.000
from miners to site managers.

00:29:10.040 --> 00:29:15.080
Much of the product is sold illegally to avoid paying taxes to the Congolese government.

00:29:16.040 --> 00:29:16.480
In Goma,

00:29:16.880 --> 00:29:20.240
we pose as traders wanting to buy smuggled Khotan.

00:29:21.480 --> 00:29:23.240
We made an appointment with traffickers.

00:29:26.320 --> 00:29:28.720
Do you want one ton, two tons, three tons?

00:29:28.880 --> 00:29:31.680
It depends on the price.
That's not a problem.

00:29:32.320 --> 00:29:36.920
The traffickers present us with different coltan samples to try and convince us.

00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:42.000
Where does that one come from, Masisi?
- Yes, Masisi.

00:29:44.160 --> 00:29:46.720
Where exactly?
- Rubaya.

00:29:50.080 --> 00:29:51.280
According to these sellers,

00:29:51.320 --> 00:29:54.160
the coltan comes from the place where we just left.

00:29:56.800 --> 00:29:58.800
90 dollars per kilo?
- Yes.

00:30:03.440 --> 00:30:05.400
This Khloetan is tax-free.

00:30:06.200 --> 00:30:06.960
At this price,

00:30:07.120 --> 00:30:11.680
the traffickers are responsible for delivering the goods across the Rwandan border.

00:30:12.480 --> 00:30:20.120
The country is regularly accused of stimulating economic growth through smuggled raw materials from the Democratic Republic of Congo.

00:30:24.240 --> 00:30:27.680
This theft takes place with the help of Congolese soldiers.

00:30:31.640 --> 00:30:32.400
Like this man,

00:30:32.680 --> 00:30:34.520
who lets the convoys pass through.

00:30:34.880 --> 00:30:37.440
Do you see coltan passing through every day?

00:30:37.600 --> 00:30:45.280
Some days 2, 3, or even 10 tons
can pass through.

00:30:45.920 --> 00:30:47.920
Like all Congolese civil servants,

00:30:48.280 --> 00:30:50.400
this soldier only gets a small salad.

00:30:51.280 --> 00:30:55.200
With coltan, I can easily earn 1000 dollars a day

00:30:56.560 --> 00:30:58.720
So everyone does it.
Yes.

00:30:58.880 --> 00:31:07.200
If traffickers come and offer me 500 or 1000 dollars
I can't refuse.

00:31:07.360 --> 00:31:15.440
I earn 80 dollars a month, so when I have the option
of getting 1000 dollars a day, it's an easy decision.

00:31:17.000 --> 00:31:20.640
The DRC is one of the 20 most corrupt countries on the planet.

00:31:21.120 --> 00:31:21.640
In total,

00:31:21.920 --> 00:31:26.240
corruption costs the Congolese state 11 billion pounds every year.

00:31:27.480 --> 00:31:29.120
Despite all of this trafficking,

00:31:29.440 --> 00:31:32.120
the mining sector drives the DRC's economy.

00:31:33.200 --> 00:31:35.160
The country's economy has grown by almost a quarter.

00:31:35.160 --> 00:31:35.600
by almost 6%

00:31:35.600 --> 00:31:37.680
in 2018,

00:31:38.080 --> 00:31:39.440
thanks to this industry.

00:31:40.840 --> 00:31:44.200
This economic success is showcased in Kinshasa,

00:31:44.600 --> 00:31:45.240
the capital,

00:31:45.640 --> 00:31:47.760
around the Boulevard d'Outre-Jouan.

00:31:52.160 --> 00:31:54.920
The 30th of June is their Independence Day,

00:31:55.520 --> 00:31:58.520
which was granted after almost a century of Belgian rule.

00:31:59.760 --> 00:32:02.360
Here in the business district we find Olivier,

00:32:02.760 --> 00:32:07.680
the young banker who moved to the Cité du Fleuve a few weeks ago with his wife Naomi.

00:32:07.680 --> 00:32:10.960
A cheesecake?
Yes, I love them.

00:32:11.120 --> 00:32:12.080
Yes, I love them too, or apple pie?

00:32:12.480 --> 00:32:15.280
9.350fc Yes, I love them too, or apple pie?

00:32:15.520 --> 00:32:17.680
They didn't exist when I was a kid.

00:32:18.280 --> 00:32:20.680
These pastries cost four pounds each,

00:32:21.200 --> 00:32:22.880
the same price as in the UK.

00:32:23.840 --> 00:32:25.280
They're a luxury in Kinshasa.

00:32:25.280 --> 00:32:26.480
5950 FC.
That's 27.78 dollars please.

00:32:26.640 --> 00:32:26.960
That's 27.78 dollars please.

00:32:27.120 --> 00:32:27.840
That's 27.78 dollars please.

00:32:28.640 --> 00:32:31.840
21 pounds is almost the country's average salary,

00:32:32.400 --> 00:32:34.440
but that doesn't seem to bother Olivier.

00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:37.440
It's cheap, it's fine.

00:32:38.880 --> 00:32:43.640
Although these well-paid executives only make up a tiny part of the population,

00:32:44.160 --> 00:32:48.440
new businesses are slowly but surely being set up in the city center.

00:32:49.920 --> 00:32:51.920
No, this isn't the one we usually use.

00:32:57.960 --> 00:33:00.440
This supermarket has adapted its stock.

00:33:01.080 --> 00:33:04.520
From coffee capsules to European cheeses to cereal,

00:33:05.120 --> 00:33:08.400
you can find everything here that is sold in rich countries.

00:33:08.440 --> 00:33:09.560
Okay,

00:33:09.840 --> 00:33:10.040
so we go.

00:33:10.040 --> 00:33:10.120
Yeah.

00:33:10.120 --> 00:33:11.040
Can we get a...

00:33:11.040 --> 00:33:11.600
Juice.

00:33:11.600 --> 00:33:12.880
Juice.

00:33:13.480 --> 00:33:17.960
But they have to pay a huge price for all of these imported products.

00:33:18.040 --> 00:33:19.640
$31,000.

00:33:19.640 --> 00:33:20.280
How many dollars?

00:33:20.480 --> 00:33:21.360
That's about

00:33:22.520 --> 00:33:26.480
$20. It's too expensive for anyone really.

00:33:26.480 --> 00:33:28.440
I can't speak for other people,

00:33:28.440 --> 00:33:28.520
but...

00:33:28.520 --> 00:33:28.600
No,

00:33:28.600 --> 00:33:28.800
