00:34:24.600 --> 00:34:24.720
But,

00:34:24.720 --> 00:34:24.840
yeah,

00:34:24.840 --> 00:34:28.760
if this didn't exist,

00:34:28.760 --> 00:34:29.560
I don't know if we'd eat.

00:34:29.560 --> 00:34:30.520
Naomi makes sure that she eats about about

00:34:30.600 --> 00:34:33.560
balanced diet because she is pregnant.

00:34:34.160 --> 00:34:34.920
It will be a boy.

00:34:35.480 --> 00:34:36.720
He's due in three months.

00:34:38.840 --> 00:34:39.720
It's a baby boy.

00:34:40.400 --> 00:34:41.400
I'm a little bit nervous,

00:34:41.480 --> 00:34:43.200
but happy at the same time.

00:34:43.360 --> 00:34:45.520
I think it's just like first time parents.

00:34:45.560 --> 00:34:52.120
We've never raised another human before.

00:34:53.200 --> 00:34:57.600
This is the perfect outcome for the couple who have had time to settle down.

00:34:59.400 --> 00:34:59.920
Thank you.

00:35:00.720 --> 00:35:03.280
I think we're done.

00:35:04.800 --> 00:35:05.640
Little by little,

00:35:05.760 --> 00:35:07.680
their apartment is becoming more homely.

00:35:17.440 --> 00:35:19.120
Heavenly Father,

00:35:19.560 --> 00:35:20.360
thank you for this meal.

00:35:20.360 --> 00:35:22.800
We thank you for this.

00:35:22.840 --> 00:35:26.280
This meal gives them a chance to consider their child's future,

00:35:26.680 --> 00:35:29.760
which will most likely be in the Democratic Republic of Congo.

00:35:29.840 --> 00:35:35.200
If he wants to become a doctor, we now
have the money to pay for his medical studies.

00:35:35.360 --> 00:35:36.960
If he wants to become a sportsman...

00:35:37.120 --> 00:35:41.600
...we will have enough money to put him in
an academy to do football or basketball...

00:35:45.520 --> 00:35:46.200
Why?

00:35:46.200 --> 00:35:48.000
Because I want him to be his own boss.

00:35:48.640 --> 00:35:52.080
And I don't want him to spend his life working for somebody else.

00:35:53.520 --> 00:35:54.240
An entrepreneur,

00:35:54.760 --> 00:35:57.520
the job that young Congolese people dream of.

00:35:58.040 --> 00:35:59.120
The job is demanding,

00:35:59.560 --> 00:36:02.080
but the success more than makes up for it.

00:36:06.160 --> 00:36:06.720
This evening,

00:36:06.960 --> 00:36:10.320
an entrepreneur is celebrating an exciting new contract.

00:36:10.920 --> 00:36:12.320
He is called Eric Monga.

00:36:13.240 --> 00:36:16.600
This business leader is also at the top of an employer's union.

00:36:17.600 --> 00:36:21.440
Let's toast to the future of our business...

00:36:21.600 --> 00:36:24.240
And the future success of your company.

00:36:24.520 --> 00:36:27.560
Eric's friends are drinking only the best champagne.

00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:29.560
They are celebrating good news.

00:36:30.160 --> 00:36:33.560
The businessman has just come back from Florida in the USA,

00:36:33.960 --> 00:36:35.320
where he met with investors.

00:36:35.640 --> 00:36:39.160
He is in the process of convincing them to fund his project,

00:36:39.480 --> 00:36:40.720
which is certainly ambitious.

00:36:41.440 --> 00:36:43.160
and which will cost upwards of

00:36:45.520 --> 00:36:50.880
He has negotiated a contract which has
gone through which I cannot disclose here.

00:36:51.120 --> 00:36:55.360
However, I can tell you that the contract
our friend just negotiated...

00:36:55.520 --> 00:36:58.080
...is worth drinking a glass of champagne for.

00:36:58.920 --> 00:37:02.920
Eric wants to construct what will be one of the Congo's largest dams.

00:37:03.360 --> 00:37:03.640
Today,

00:37:03.760 --> 00:37:07.880
less than one in five Congolese people are connected to the electricity network.

00:37:08.640 --> 00:37:11.880
Eric is hoping to fill part of this gap with this new project.

00:37:12.320 --> 00:37:16.880
For every problem we face, there is
a business opportunity that comes with it.

00:37:17.040 --> 00:37:26.240
People must eat, they must get dressed and now,
we want to give electricity to the people next year.

00:37:28.440 --> 00:37:28.960
In time,

00:37:29.160 --> 00:37:34.160
Eric will improve the living conditions for some of his 81 million fellow citizens.

00:37:37.120 --> 00:37:40.880
The businessman is from Lumbumbashi in the south of the Congo.

00:37:41.600 --> 00:37:47.040
He has made his fortune by creating a company specializing in the analysis of minerals.

00:37:51.120 --> 00:37:56.240
The entrepreneur is leaving this morning for an expedition on the site of his future dam.

00:37:56.240 --> 00:37:58.640
Hey Isaac, let's go!

00:38:02.480 --> 00:38:04.880
It is 350 kilometers away.

00:38:05.840 --> 00:38:08.160
Eric is looking to check the river's flow rate.

00:38:10.320 --> 00:38:12.360
But the road is extremely dangerous,

00:38:12.640 --> 00:38:14.760
and Eric asks his colleagues to be careful.

00:38:16.240 --> 00:38:17.760
We are waiting for you in Kalera.

00:38:17.920 --> 00:38:20.160
Don't forget that you have to make
the journey during the day.

00:38:20.320 --> 00:38:21.680
You wouldn't want to drive at night.

00:38:22.520 --> 00:38:23.640
There are no lights,

00:38:23.960 --> 00:38:25.160
very little signage,

00:38:25.360 --> 00:38:26.720
and potholes everywhere.

00:38:27.920 --> 00:38:29.680
The National Road 1 highway,

00:38:30.160 --> 00:38:31.480
which crosses Katanga,

00:38:31.800 --> 00:38:33.920
is one of the most deadly roads in the country.

00:38:34.920 --> 00:38:41.400
Many lorries transporting minerals and chemical products used in the mining industry use this road every day.

00:38:41.680 --> 00:38:44.320
Acid, acid, acid.

00:38:45.680 --> 00:38:52.440
Drivers on this road will take any risks necessary to ensure timely delivery of their precious merchandise.

00:38:53.520 --> 00:38:58.000
Roads in the Congo are deadly,
there are a lot of accidents.

00:38:58.160 --> 00:39:02.400
There are some crazy drivers.

00:39:04.760 --> 00:39:09.880
Three of the 11 passengers in this vehicle were just killed just a few hours ago.

00:39:11.000 --> 00:39:12.840
But that doesn't affect these drivers.

00:39:13.240 --> 00:39:14.360
Eric is worried.

00:39:14.840 --> 00:39:18.640
A high-speed car suddenly comes by a little too close.

00:39:20.080 --> 00:39:21.120
What's going on?

00:39:21.280 --> 00:39:24.880
There is a man behind me who wants to overtake
but he's crazy...

00:39:25.040 --> 00:39:28.880
He's being really impatient
and putting me in danger.

00:39:29.560 --> 00:39:31.280
Despite the low visibility,

00:39:31.520 --> 00:39:32.840
the driver goes for it.

00:39:35.200 --> 00:39:37.040
It looks like he is fleeing the police.

00:39:39.040 --> 00:39:43.920
It's just a small spat but he's got nothing to
gain other than putting our lives in danger...

00:39:45.280 --> 00:39:47.400
After three hours of difficult driving,

00:39:47.840 --> 00:39:50.080
Eric can finally breathe a sigh of relief.

00:39:50.760 --> 00:39:53.960
He leaves the National Road 1 highway to take a long

00:39:54.600 --> 00:39:55.480
100-kilometer track,

00:39:55.760 --> 00:39:57.520
which is used far less frequently.

00:39:58.640 --> 00:39:59.960
The area where he hopes to

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:02.720
to set up his dam is currently very remote.

00:40:03.640 --> 00:40:04.880
In order to construct it,

00:40:05.080 --> 00:40:07.320
he will have to bring workers in from far away.

00:40:07.960 --> 00:40:09.600
But the challenge is worth it.

00:40:11.680 --> 00:40:17.360
It's going to earn me almost 1 million
dollars per month, it's a nice paycheck!

00:40:17.520 --> 00:40:21.120
And that...
Oh, sorry, that's the ditch!

00:40:23.560 --> 00:40:24.320
In the meantime,

00:40:24.520 --> 00:40:27.400
Eric has set up a small camp in the middle of nowhere,

00:40:27.800 --> 00:40:29.640
which hosts a dozen engineers.

00:40:33.520 --> 00:40:36.240
Hello.
Is everything ok here?

00:40:38.840 --> 00:40:42.400
The employees have been living here for a year completely alone.

00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:44.320
They have a water tank,

00:40:44.600 --> 00:40:47.360
a generator and a small shed for tools.

00:40:51.040 --> 00:40:55.200
When does the sun set here?
At around 6:15.

00:40:55.520 --> 00:41:00.160
So we still have 40 minutes,
I really need to see the water level today.

00:41:02.200 --> 00:41:04.000
Despite being tired from traveling,

00:41:04.080 --> 00:41:06.400
this businessman can't waste any time.

00:41:06.840 --> 00:41:09.600
He leads his team to the bank of the Lofira River,

00:41:10.040 --> 00:41:11.440
which runs through the dam.

00:41:12.480 --> 00:41:14.880
Eric checks the height and the speed of the water.

00:41:17.840 --> 00:41:19.760
And how much did you say it was there?

00:41:19.920 --> 00:41:22.560
The water level is 1 metre 63.

00:41:22.720 --> 00:41:25.520
1 metre 63 compared to the scale over there.

00:41:26.680 --> 00:41:31.120
The project has already successfully passed all of the feasibility tests.

00:41:31.760 --> 00:41:37.280
We are at around 735 metres
and the dam will be 830 metres.

00:41:38.480 --> 00:41:44.800
The water will stop at the first level there,
almost on the edge of the horizon over there...

00:41:44.960 --> 00:41:47.440
...that will all be a lake.

00:41:47.680 --> 00:41:50.720
The project will be one of the five largest in the Congo.

00:41:51.160 --> 00:41:52.600
With a height of 90 meters,

00:41:52.760 --> 00:41:55.360
it will produce 150 megawatts of power,

00:41:55.400 --> 00:41:56.400
which we'll be able to use to power the entire Congo.

00:41:56.480 --> 00:41:59.600
to provide 500,000 people with electricity.

00:42:00.040 --> 00:42:03.400
It will supply the equivalent of the population of Manchester.

00:42:04.120 --> 00:42:10.760
The dam's construction is expected to create almost 3,000 jobs and boost the region's economy.

00:42:11.200 --> 00:42:15.600
We are constructing something permanent
and which will serve an entire community..

00:42:15.760 --> 00:42:23.120
.bringing joy for all of the locals who
just needed this energy in order to develop.

00:42:23.120 --> 00:42:26.480
Several large investors, notably american’s

00:42:26.480 --> 00:42:28.600
have registered their interest in the project.

00:42:28.840 --> 00:42:34.240
Eric hopes to gather the 250 million pounds needed for the project in the next three years.

00:42:34.760 --> 00:42:36.200
Upon returning to the camp,

00:42:36.280 --> 00:42:38.320
he has a small surprise for his team.

00:42:38.320 --> 00:42:43.120
We have a saying here that goes 'Koutoumba
and buouavakila' which means 'drink and talk!'

00:42:44.360 --> 00:42:48.760
He has asked his cook to prepare a celebratory meal of traditional dishes.

00:42:49.840 --> 00:42:53.120
That's Ngai Ngai grown in Boiri.

00:42:53.280 --> 00:42:54.960
It's very close to here.

00:42:55.120 --> 00:42:59.440
These are amaranths...

00:43:00.240 --> 00:43:02.240
Also grown in Boiri.

00:43:05.400 --> 00:43:05.680
Thank you.

00:43:05.680 --> 00:43:07.400
Eric believes that in this country,

00:43:07.840 --> 00:43:09.760
one of the least developed in the world,

00:43:10.040 --> 00:43:12.520
there are various opportunities for success.

00:43:13.280 --> 00:43:16.200
You just need to dare to take a leap and get started.

00:43:17.920 --> 00:43:20.960
We have seen a lot of people coming to the Congo...

00:43:21.120 --> 00:43:27.200
.going to where it's difficult, where there's
nothing and succeeding. And why can't I?

00:43:28.560 --> 00:43:30.320
That's the Congo...

00:43:30.480 --> 00:43:36.320
You can wake up poor and the next day,
you will be rich because you have worked hard.

00:43:38.080 --> 00:43:41.960
Inspired by the boldness and success of entrepreneurs like Eric,

00:43:42.400 --> 00:43:48.320
more and more Congolese people are throwing themselves into the world of business in a hope to escape poverty.

00:43:50.720 --> 00:43:55.080
And this dream motivates thousands of women in Kinshasa every day.

00:43:58.520 --> 00:43:59.880
They come at 4 a.m.

00:43:59.960 --> 00:44:03.920
from all parts of the city to stock up on bread from this wholesaler.

00:44:04.720 --> 00:44:07.320
They buy whatever they can to make a living that day.

00:44:12.200 --> 00:44:15.000
Marie comes here every day for the 6 a.m.

00:44:15.040 --> 00:44:15.440
batch.

00:44:18.400 --> 00:44:19.760
I'll take two tubs.

00:44:22.680 --> 00:44:29.680
Marie was widowed six months ago and therefore has the huge responsibility of bringing enough home to feed her whole family.

00:44:31.120 --> 00:44:33.040
Wait, give me that please.

00:44:33.920 --> 00:44:38.240
It's not too heavy for me, I'm used
to carrying it all, it's my job.

00:44:40.760 --> 00:44:44.600
Marie is carrying more than 15 kilograms of goods on her head.

00:44:45.240 --> 00:44:48.440
She sets up her stall in a strategic location every day,

00:44:48.800 --> 00:44:50.480
which will get her the most clients.

00:44:56.560 --> 00:44:58.720
I'll have a cake.
How much is it?

00:44:58.880 --> 00:45:01.440
The cake is 300 francs.
- Ok, I will take one.

00:45:03.920 --> 00:45:07.680
I am going to give you two.
I'll give you two because you're a little thin.

00:45:07.840 --> 00:45:09.440
Oh, thank you very much.

00:45:09.600 --> 00:45:12.960
I just bought some bread from Marie
because I pass by her stand.

00:45:13.120 --> 00:45:18.320
I really like it, it's clean and she
takes good care of her stand.

00:45:19.000 --> 00:45:21.440
Thanks to her smile and her kindness,

00:45:21.560 --> 00:45:24.040
Marie usually attracts a lot of customers.

00:45:24.880 --> 00:45:27.920
It's a good day, it's going well!

00:45:29.440 --> 00:45:31.320
Marie earns 50 pounds per day,

00:45:31.720 --> 00:45:33.320
thanks to this little stand.

00:45:33.960 --> 00:45:38.040
She believes in her business and dreams of opening other stands like this one.

00:45:38.560 --> 00:45:41.640
She even allows herself to imagine making a fortune.

00:45:42.000 --> 00:45:43.840
You need to know how to manage.

00:45:44.000 --> 00:45:47.360
If you know how to manage your business well,
you can become a millionaire.

00:45:47.520 --> 00:45:50.640
If you don't know how to manage it,
you will never be able to become a millionaire.

00:45:50.800 --> 00:45:53.680
You must be smart, think hard,
and manage your business well.

00:45:54.520 --> 00:45:56.280
But there's still a long way to go,

00:45:56.680 --> 00:46:01.160
because Marie's net profit for a day's work is just 15 pounds.

00:46:01.920 --> 00:46:03.760
and a third of this sum needs to go to the bank.

00:46:03.880 --> 00:46:07.120
towards renting a small apartment with a kitchen on the landing.

00:46:12.000 --> 00:46:13.760
This is Fumbwa...

00:46:14.000 --> 00:46:17.440
I put peanut butter, garlic, chili, onions and fish in

00:46:18.240 --> 00:46:21.040
I put peanut butter, garlic, chili, onions and fish in

00:46:22.480 --> 00:46:23.040
Inside,

00:46:23.240 --> 00:46:24.360
there is a single room,

00:46:24.520 --> 00:46:28.840
which is used as a bedroom and living room for Marie and her daughter.

00:46:29.800 --> 00:46:32.240
Sarah is the youngest of her five children.

00:46:33.440 --> 00:46:40.880
That's Deborah and Israel,
who sat his bac exam today.

00:46:44.640 --> 00:46:47.720
With a salary higher than 350 pounds per month,

00:46:47.800 --> 00:46:49.720
Marie could live in a bigger apartment.

00:46:50.600 --> 00:46:55.400
But she would rather save money on her housing in order to fund her children's studies.

00:46:58.960 --> 00:47:02.320
I need to pay for my children's schooling
all on my own.

00:47:02.480 --> 00:47:05.520
I had to pay for Deborah and Israel's
in the same year.

00:47:06.320 --> 00:47:11.200
You realise I'm paying school fees
for two children at the same time..

00:47:11.600 --> 00:47:14.320
...and I still have another daughter Marjorie.

00:47:14.480 --> 00:47:20.080
I'm also going to start paying for
Josepha and Jordie, and I'm all alone.

00:47:21.080 --> 00:47:23.920
Their schooling costs her 25 pounds per month,

00:47:24.520 --> 00:47:28.720
but it will give them the tools they need to encourage them to dream big too.

00:47:35.120 --> 00:47:40.480
I could become a millionaire like some people are,
but that will only happen if God wills it.

00:47:40.640 --> 00:47:43.840
If he helps me, it will happen.

00:47:45.800 --> 00:47:46.320
Like 90%

00:47:46.760 --> 00:47:47.920
of Congolese people,

00:47:48.160 --> 00:47:50.600
Marie and her daughter Sarah are Christians.

00:47:51.520 --> 00:47:53.960
They follow the evangelical denomination.

00:47:55.120 --> 00:47:57.760
The shopkeeper visits a temple three times a week.

00:47:58.360 --> 00:48:00.960
She thanks God for having spared her from poverty.

00:48:05.040 --> 00:48:10.960
God is very important to me.
I have this life thanks to Him.

00:48:12.040 --> 00:48:14.400
Evangelical churches thrive in the Congo,

00:48:14.800 --> 00:48:17.160
much like in many other African countries.

00:48:17.720 --> 00:48:22.800
And by exploiting the Congolese people's strong faith and sometimes their naivety,

00:48:23.480 --> 00:48:26.240
some religious leaders have become millionaires.

00:48:31.520 --> 00:48:33.280
This Sunday morning in Kinshasa,

00:48:33.720 --> 00:48:38.000
all of the city's usually very busy main streets are strangely deserted.

00:48:41.720 --> 00:48:42.320
Since dawn,

00:48:42.640 --> 00:48:47.800
tens of thousands of people have been heading towards the largest stadium in Central Africa.

00:48:52.800 --> 00:48:55.280
Go go go!
You have to go over there.

00:48:55.960 --> 00:49:01.080
80,000 attendees are not there for a football match or a huge concert.

00:49:01.720 --> 00:49:05.480
They have come to hear a speech from a man who sells a juice,

00:49:05.720 --> 00:49:08.720
which supposedly has extraordinary powers.

00:49:10.000 --> 00:49:12.560
We always believe in the
prophet Khonde's miracles.

00:49:12.720 --> 00:49:15.680
On my deathbed I had a drink, a glass of juice.

00:49:15.840 --> 00:49:20.640
And my stomach was like that, greenish,
and it went down straight away.

00:49:20.800 --> 00:49:25.440
I am living proof:
he is a prophet, he is a prophet

00:49:33.960 --> 00:49:34.840
There are cameramen,

00:49:35.440 --> 00:49:36.240
photographers,

00:49:36.960 --> 00:49:37.640
cheerleaders.

00:49:39.040 --> 00:49:40.120
Policemen on alert.

00:49:40.960 --> 00:49:42.600
It's the biggest event of the year.

00:49:43.440 --> 00:49:46.240
It is also being broadcast live on television.

00:49:49.680 --> 00:49:53.080
The star everyone is waiting for is called The Prophet.

00:49:53.760 --> 00:49:56.280
He lives a few kilometers away from the stadium.

00:49:57.360 --> 00:49:59.880
We find him at his home where his escort is.

00:50:00.080 --> 00:50:02.480
Already ready and dressed impeccably,

00:50:03.200 --> 00:50:06.440
his bodyguards are also his disciples.

00:50:06.880 --> 00:50:13.600
The prophet Khonde is really a man of God,
one of His messengers..

00:50:13.760 --> 00:50:18.000
He really does everything - everything
that Jesus does he does as well.

00:50:18.160 --> 00:50:24.480
He is truly our prophet
and God sent him to our country.

00:50:24.920 --> 00:50:27.880
The prophet Conde is this man with a floral shirt.

00:50:28.520 --> 00:50:29.040
Dominique,

00:50:29.120 --> 00:50:29.760
his first name.

00:50:30.120 --> 00:50:34.160
created a Christian church in the Congo which has five million followers.

00:50:34.680 --> 00:50:37.360
It is a success story that could make people jealous.

